CAT = "hkle1Misconduct"; SEG = "MIS"
Q = [
("A company director learns of an unannounced profit warning and sells his shares. This is:",
 "Insider dealing", ["Price rigging", "False trading", "Stock market manipulation"],
 "Dealing while in possession of inside information as a person connected with the corporation is insider dealing under Parts XIII and XIV of the SFO."),
("A trader buys and sells the same shares between accounts she controls to make the stock look busy. This is:",
 "False trading", ["Insider dealing", "Front running", "Best execution"],
 "Creating a false or misleading appearance of active trading, for example by wash trades with no change in beneficial ownership, is false trading."),
("A wash sale that involves no change in beneficial ownership, done to affect a stock's price, is the market misconduct of:",
 "Price rigging", ["Insider dealing", "Disclosure of inside information", "Unsolicited calling"],
 "Price rigging covers wash sales and fictitious or artificial transactions that maintain, raise, lower or stabilise a price."),
("Spreading a false rumour likely to push a share price up, knowing it is false, is:",
 "Disclosing false information", ["Best execution", "Fair allocation of shares", "Price stabilisation after an IPO"],
 "Disclosing false or misleading information that is likely to induce transactions, knowing or being reckless as to its falsity, is market misconduct."),
("For the same market misconduct, the SFO lets the authorities use MMT proceedings and criminal prosecution:",
 "Only one of the two", ["Both, one after the other", "Always both at the same time", "Neither; HKEX decides"],
 "The SFO's dual civil and criminal regime has double jeopardy protection: once MMT proceedings or criminal proceedings are started for conduct, the other route cannot be used for the same conduct."),
("The Market Misconduct Tribunal can make a cold shoulder order, which:",
 "Bars a person from dealing", ["Sends a person to prison", "Winds up the listed company", "Revokes the stock's listing"],
 "A cold shoulder order bars the person, without court leave, from dealing in securities and futures in Hong Kong for up to five years. The MMT cannot impose prison."),
("The MMT orders a director not to be a director of a listed company for a period. This is a:",
 "Disqualification order", ["Cold shoulder order", "Restriction notice", "Public reprimand by the SFC"],
 "A disqualification order stops the person from being a director or involved in managing a listed corporation without court leave for up to five years."),
("An investor who lost money because of someone's market misconduct may:",
 "Sue for compensation", ["Claim from the stock exchange", "Get money only from the SFC", "Do nothing under the SFO"],
 "The SFO gives a private right of civil action for pecuniary loss caused by market misconduct, against the person who committed it."),
("Under the SFO, an unsolicited call is generally prohibited when it is made to:",
 "Get someone to buy securities", ["Confirm a client's address", "Answer the client's own question", "Remind a client of a margin call"],
 "Section 174 bars making unsolicited calls (visits or oral communications without express invitation) to induce a person to enter into agreements on securities, futures or leveraged FX, subject to exclusions."),
("A broker trades excessively in a client's discretionary account mainly to earn commission. This is:",
 "Churning", ["Hedging", "Netting", "Rebalancing"],
 "Excessive trading for commission rather than the client's benefit is churning, an improper trading practice and a breach of the Code."),
("A fund manager arranges for a friend to hold shares for him to hide his own interest. This is called:",
 "Warehousing", ["Short selling", "Averaging down", "Market making"],
 "Warehousing or parking places shares with others to conceal the true holder, which can breach disclosure of interests and market misconduct rules."),
("A group buys cheap shares, hypes them on social media and sells to new buyers as the price rises. This scheme is known as:",
 "Ramp and dump", ["Dollar cost averaging", "Pair trading", "Index tracking"],
 "Ramp and dump (pump and dump) schemes ramp up a stock's price with misleading promotion and then sell to investors drawn in, often leaving them with heavy losses."),
("Which is a typical reason for the SFC to take enforcement action against a licensed person?",
 "Taking client money", ["Charging a fair commission", "Filing returns on time", "Recording phone orders"],
 "Enforcement actions commonly follow misconduct such as misappropriation, market misconduct, internal control failures and misleading clients."),
("Who decides whether to bring criminal market misconduct cases on indictment?",
 "The Department of Justice", ["HKEX's Listing Committee", "The Takeovers Panel", "The Investor Compensation Company"],
 "Indictable offences, including serious market misconduct offences under Part XIV, are prosecuted by the Department of Justice; the SFC can prosecute summary offences itself."),
]
